# Preserve `.keep` files

`.keep` files may exist only to keep a directory tracked in git.

- Never delete a `.keep` file unless user explicitly asks.
- If real files are added to that directory, deleting `.keep` is allowed.
- Be extra careful when staging with `git add -A` or deleting generated assets.
- If a `.keep` file is the only tracked file in a directory, preserve it by default.
